    <text>
        <body>
            <div xml:id="d86">

                <pb facs="0234" n="138" sameAs="frus:frus1872p1/pg138"/>

                <head>No. 86.<lb/><hi rendition="#italic">Mr. Fish
                        to Mr. Low.</hi></head>
                <opener>
                    <dateline rendition="#float-right"><placeName><hi rendition="#small-caps"
                                >Department of State</hi>,<lb/><hi rendition="#italic"
                                >Washington</hi></placeName>, <date calendar="gregorian"
                            when="1872-10-04"><hi rendition="#italic">October</hi> 4,
                        1872</date>.</dateline>
                    <seg rendition="#float-left">No. 101.]</seg>
                </opener>
                <p><hi rendition="#small-caps">Sir</hi>: Your dispatch No. 172, under date of 12th
                    July last, relating to the departure of thirty Chinese youths for education in
                    the United States, and bespeaking my good offices in their behalf at the request
                    of Li Hung Chang, has been received. The arrival of these young men is regarded
                    with interest, and it will give me pleasure to manifest my friendly feeling for
                    them should a proper occasion offer.</p>
                <p>I am, &amp;c,</p>
                <closer>
                    <signed>HAMILTON FISH.</signed>
                </closer>
            </div>
        </body>
    </text>
